>> title: Kabocha no Nimono
>> category: Vegetables & Sides
>> tags: japanese, kabocha, squash, dashi, simmered, make ahead, vegetarian
>> counters: Japanese Home Cooking
>> aka: かぼちゃの煮物, kabocha no nimono, kabocha no nimono, かぼちゃの煮付け, simmered pumpkin, simmered kabocha squash, Japanese squash side
>> pairs-with: dashi, gohan
>> servings: 4
>> time: 40 min
>> slack: forgiving — it does not come back from a rolling boil, which drops the flesh off the skin and leaves you with soup
>> step.1: The twenty minutes of cooling at the end is part of it. 煮物 ratio: dashi 10 : soy 1 : mirin 1 : sake 1.
>> step.2: arrange skin down, pour over
>> step.3: simmer 15 min under a drop lid
>> step.4: cool in the liquid 20 min

Four ingredients, one pot, twenty minutes on the heat, and twenty off it that most written versions leave out.

Arrange @kabocha{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; in 2-inch pieces, skin on, corners pared off) skin-side down in one layer in a #wide saucepan{} and pour @dashi{1 1/4%cups}(300 mL; or 1 1/4 cups water and 1/2 tsp dashi granules), @soy sauce{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @mirin{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @sake{2%Tbs}(30 mL) and @sugar{1%Tbs} over it.

Lay a drop lid straight onto @&(~1)kabocha{} — paper cut to the pan with a hole in it — and ~simmer{15%min} at a bare bubble, until a skewer goes through.

Take @&(~1)pan{} off the heat and leave it to ~cool{20%min} in its own liquid without lifting anything out.
